From: Dan Lapid <dlapid@cloudflare.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Propagate coverage info through link_deps

A crate's `link_deps` are linked into the binary like its `deps`, so the
instrumented sources and coverage metadata of the C++ libraries listed
there are part of the binary's coverage too. Bazel's LCOV merger keeps
only the sources named in the test's instrumented-files manifest, so
without this the C++ half of a Rust binary is dropped from the report.
---
 rust/private/rustc.bzl | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/rust/private/rustc.bzl b/rust/private/rustc.bzl
--- a/rust/private/rustc.bzl
+++ b/rust/private/rustc.bzl
@@ -2170,7 +2170,7 @@ def rustc_compile_action(
     executable = crate_info.output if crate_info.type == "bin" or crate_info.is_test else None
 
     instrumented_files_kwargs = {
-        "dependency_attributes": ["deps", "crate"],
+        "dependency_attributes": ["deps", "link_deps", "crate"],
         "extensions": ["rs"],
         "source_attributes": ["srcs"],
     }
